Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Rebased onto master (which merged an overlapping pull-signal blockers model);
adopts that model as the base and layers a fail-closed merge VERDICT on top.
READ + verdict only — the shepherd still never merges and never resolves threads.

Agnostic actor classification (by MECHANISM, no hardcoded bot-name list; unknown
actors default to BLOCKING so a new/unnamable review bot can't cause a
false-clean):
- Threads: any unresolved, non-outdated review thread blocks, author-agnostic
  (pr-shepherd.actionableComments drops the author filter; the verdict counts raw
  unresolved threads).
- Checks/status: any failing/missing/skipped/pending required check OR a failing
  bot-status comment (buildBotStatusBlockers) → BLOCKED-CHECKS, no name knowledge.
- Direct comments: a NON-HUMAN comment (GraphQL author.__typename==Bot or a
  [bot] login; readIssueComments/readReviews now surface authorTypename) newer
  than the last head push blocks — unless on an INVERTED suppression allowlist
  (STATUS_BOT_LOGINS: known status/deploy/quality bots whose gate blocks via
  checks). Every other bot, known or unknown, is actionable.

Unique additions over master's model:
- adapter.readReviews (review-at-head oid, #365) + readHeadCommitTime (settle
  window anchor).
- pr-pull.computeVerdict: single fail-closed verdict enum
  (UNKNOWN > BLOCKED-CONFLICT > BEHIND > BLOCKED-CHECKS > BLOCKED-THREADS >
  REVIEW-PENDING > CLEAN-MERGEABLE) consuming master's raw signals plus
  review-at-head, settle window, torn-read, and UNKNOWN-on-unreadable.

False-clean fixes: F1 CLEAN only from an explicitly-good mergeStateStatus; F2
raw unresolved-thread count; F3 settle window anchored to head-push (fresh green
PR is REVIEW-PENDING, CLEAN needs a known push time); F5 bot comment anchored to
head-push not agent chatter. F4 left as filed Tier-2.

Tests: full verdict precedence + agnostic (unknown-bot thread/comment, unnamed
failing check, suppressed informational comment) + F1/F2/F3/F5 + #365/#353 +
fail-closed + torn-read, via injected deps. Corrected the acceptance test that
codified the #365 bug.

Issues: c01936be, 35ee8d78

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
